# Print which reviews this branch owes, before it becomes a PR.
#
# Reporting, not blocking: nothing here can tell whether a review actually
# happened, only which ones the table in CLAUDE.md requires. The point is that
# the answer arrives unprompted. The rule was "non-trivial changes get
# reviewed" and was violated seven PRs running; it became a table, and the
# table was then skipped three more times — because running the grep was still
# something a person had to remember.
#
# `|| ...` rather than a bare call because this must not block a push. But a
# bare `|| true` swallowed a throw as well as a non-zero exit: `blastRadius()`
# throws when it cannot find the list in docs/GIT.md, and because the headline
# prints before that, the output read as an ordinary short run with no triggers
# owed. Measured — reword the heading and all four rows and the summary vanish,
# exit 0. Silent under-reporting is the one direction this tool must never fail
# in, so the failure gets a line of its own.
node tools/review-triggers.ts ||
  echo "  !!  review-triggers FAILED — which reviews are owed is UNKNOWN. Run 'pnpm review-triggers'." 
